Falsifies `system_tests::user::raw_mode_tests::a_badged_copy_of_the_terminal_reads_keystrokes_and_cannot_type_them`.

Architecture: all three (the change is in a userspace component, `components/src/line_editor.rs`,
built for every ISA from one source; the table it reads is `terminal_contract::admits`, which
nife takes from `nifeos/terminal_contract` by rev).

The defect this restores is the one milestone 709 closes: the boot line discipline served every
request the same whatever the badge on the capability that sent it, so a `graphical_terminal`
session holding a copy of its endpoint could `OPERATION_BYTES` a command line into the queue the boot shell
reads with `OPERATION_READLINE`. The patch lets the raw-only badge past the serve loop's
allowlist whole (`badge == proto::RAW_ONLY_BADGE ||` ahead of `proto::admits`), which is that
guard removed for this badge.

Expected to fail: `assert_eq!(r[0], BAD_REQUEST, "a badged holder's OPERATION_BYTES was served (r0 = 0):
it can type a line the boot shell reads")`, the first assertion in the test. Under the patch the
discipline answers `0` and queues `ls`.

The patch sits in `line_editor`'s serve loop because the table itself left the tree with
`terminal_contract`. Replayed red on aarch64 on 2026-11-22 (UTC), at the same first assertion.

diff --git a/components/src/line_editor.rs b/components/src/line_editor.rs
index 71b08e4ce..105113804 100644
--- a/components/src/line_editor.rs
+++ b/components/src/line_editor.rs
@@ -159,7 +159,7 @@ fn start(mode: u64, control: u64, start: u64) -> ! {
             reply(slot, proto::BAD_REQUEST, 0);
             continue;
         };
-        if !proto::admits(badge, operation) {
+        if !(badge == proto::RAW_ONLY_BADGE || proto::admits(badge, operation)) {
             reply(slot, proto::BAD_REQUEST, 0);
             continue;
         }
